{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.762149Z","id":"591fd6f4ceec720babe37225eab0c303d4912572354ec8d4559a56c88b99b909","body":{"detail":"resolve() calls valid_install on $CLAX_HOME/bin/<pin> on every invocation (lines 518-524), and valid_install (lines 303-314) computes the sha256 of the binary and then runs `clax --version` under a 5 s bound. For hooks that is per event: SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit (each prompt), Stop, PreToolUse/PostToolUse AskUserQuestion, the mcp__.*clax.* PostToolUse call-id hook and the throttled tool-hook.sh, all with 5-10 s harness timeouts (plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json). A current clax binary is about 49 MB; `shasum -a 256` of one took 0.13 s here, before the --version spawn. The same script is copied to plugins/clax, plugins/clax-grok and plugins/pi.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":524},"content_hash":"2ac80e731850d49686a0080b00c7ffccdd53f536f90759879481bdcf60b88d46"},"suggested_fix":"Have hooks trust a managed install whose clax.sha256 record exists and whose binary's size and mtime match values recorded at install (a cheap stat), keeping the full hash and --version check for MCP and CLI modes, or for hooks only when the stat check fails.","summary":"Every hook run with a managed install hashes the whole clax binary and runs its --version before the hook starts","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:34.629989Z","id":"1971c65622da8aba01158d11fcd5c304eaeeaf26ace549cd47a1899501457a1b","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-clax.sh:518-519 calls valid_install \"$dest\" unconditionally once no override applies; valid_install (lines 303-314) runs sha256_of on the binary then check_bin, which spawns `--version` under PROBE_SECS. Hook mode only skips installing (may=\"\"), not the check. `md5 -q` of plugins/{clax,clax-grok,pi,claude-code}/scripts/ensure-clax.sh all print 52b200130e9271cd9ad5125f50e0db07, so the copies are identical. Performance suggestion; kind fits.","kind":"comment","references":"591fd6f4ceec720babe37225eab0c303d4912572354ec8d4559a56c88b99b909","summary":"confirmed: resolve() runs valid_install (full sha256 plus --version) on every hook invocation","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:15:57.083265Z","id":"ddbe9a6361d1010397a88f5342579c317f6e04a2bbfd1afa0778f7af0470dc71","body":{"detail":"The header of scripts/ensure-clax.sh (lines 26-30) makes it a contract that the managed binary's hash is checked before the binary runs, in every mode. Skipping that per hook trades that contract for latency, so it is not changed here.\n\nOptions:\n(a) Keep the check in every mode (today): about 0.13 s of hashing a 49 MB binary plus one `clax --version` spawn per hook event.\n(b) At install, and whenever a full check passes in mcp/cli/print mode, write `clax.stat` beside `clax.sha256` (size, mtime and inode, via `stat -f` on macOS and `stat -c` on Linux, written to a temporary file and renamed); hook mode runs the binary when that record exists and matches, and does the full check otherwise. A replaced or truncated binary changes size, mtime or inode, so the check still catches the damage cases the hash catches in practice; anyone who can rewrite the binary can rewrite clax.sha256 too, so the hash is a corruption check, not a security boundary. The case at scripts/test-ensure-clax.sh:787 that lists the install directory as `clax clax.sha256` gains `clax.stat`.\n(c) Hook mode skips only the --version spawn and keeps the hash.\n\nRecommendation: (b), keeping the full check for mcp, cli, print and which modes. The same edit goes to scripts/ensure-clax.sh and its four copies under plugins/*/scripts/ (scripts/test-plugins.sh:294-298 checks they match).","kind":"comment","references":"591fd6f4ceec720babe37225eab0c303d4912572354ec8d4559a56c88b99b909","summary":"Needs the owner's call: whether hooks may run the managed clax without the sha256 and --version check before it runs","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
